1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:08,484
A BBC correspondent who had covered wars once said of this story: I could handle war zones, but I could not handle this.

2
00:00:08,484 --> 00:00:10,589
What shook him was not gunfire.

3
00:00:10,589 --> 00:00:14,733
It was a playground of children, and what they said they saw.

4
00:00:15,199 --> 00:00:18,944
Friday, sixteenth of September, nineteen ninety-four.

5
00:00:18,944 --> 00:00:20,003
Ruwa, Zimbabwe.

6
00:00:20,003 --> 00:00:29,399
Sixty-two children say a silver disc came down into the brush beside their school, and that small figures in black stepped out of it.

7
00:00:29,866 --> 00:00:30,728
No wreckage.

8
00:00:30,728 --> 00:00:32,738
No photographs of the craft.

9
00:00:32,738 --> 00:00:33,958
No official file.

10
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:41,569
All that exists is testimony, and the testimony was recorded again and again, on tape, in the weeks after.

11
00:00:41,569 --> 00:00:43,866
So tonight, we open the archive.

12
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,900
Tape zero, the radio.

13
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,244
Tape one, the BBC.

14
00:00:47,244 --> 00:00:49,109
Tape two, the researcher.

15
00:00:49,109 --> 00:00:51,647
Tape three, the Harvard professor.

16
00:00:51,647 --> 00:00:54,184
Tape four, a streaming confession.

17
00:00:54,184 --> 00:00:56,199
Tape five, thirty years on.

18
00:00:56,666 --> 00:00:58,349
And here is the question.

19
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:02,792
As the tapes go on, does the story get clearer, or does it change?

20
00:01:02,792 --> 00:01:03,533
Press play.

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:08,693
Tape zero.

22
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:11,400
Wednesday, the fourteenth of September.

23
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,580
Two days earlier.

24
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:16,605
At night, a fireball crossed the sky over southern Africa.

25
00:01:16,605 --> 00:01:17,785
Thousands saw it.

26
00:01:17,785 --> 00:01:20,700
Many were sure it was something unearthly.

27
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:26,195
The national radio station asked listeners to phone in and describe it.

28
00:01:26,195 --> 00:01:29,879
The airwaves filled with strange lights and rumours.

29
00:01:29,879 --> 00:01:31,366
A country was primed.

30
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:34,794
The likely culprit was far more ordinary.

31
00:01:34,794 --> 00:01:40,211
A booster from a Russian rocket, re-entering the atmosphere and burning up.

32
00:01:40,211 --> 00:01:44,400
The BBC's text service reported exactly that the next day.

33
00:01:44,866 --> 00:01:48,715
But a rocket does not make a headline like a flying saucer.

34
00:01:48,715 --> 00:01:55,500
A newspaper gave it a single sentence, and the story that caught people's imagination was the other one.

35
00:01:55,966 --> 00:02:01,868
Ariel School was a private school in Ruwa, about twenty-two kilometres from Harare.

36
00:02:01,868 --> 00:02:04,926
Many pupils came from comfortable families.

37
00:02:04,926 --> 00:02:07,699
Their parents had heard the radio, too.

38
00:02:08,166 --> 00:02:17,685
So on that Friday, two mornings after the fireball, the children walked into school with a night sky full of rumours still ringing in their ears.

39
00:02:17,685 --> 00:02:18,866
Keep that in mind.

40
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:20,494
Mid-morning break.

41
00:02:20,494 --> 00:02:22,817
The teachers are in a staff meeting.

42
00:02:22,817 --> 00:02:25,333
The playground belongs to the children.

43
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,066
About ten o'clock.

44
00:02:27,066 --> 00:02:33,048
The children are outside, and the only adult nearby is a woman running the tuck shop.

45
00:02:33,048 --> 00:02:37,833
Then, some of them say, a silvery object slides down out of the sky.

46
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,764
Their accounts agree on the outline.

47
00:02:40,764 --> 00:02:46,515
A disc, silver, silent, coming down into the small trees at the edge of the grounds.

48
00:02:46,515 --> 00:02:49,733
Perhaps a hundred metres from where they stood.

49
00:02:50,199 --> 00:02:53,496
For about fifteen minutes, they say, it stayed there.

50
00:02:53,496 --> 00:02:54,616
Some children ran.

51
00:02:54,616 --> 00:02:57,166
The older ones, they say, stayed to look.

52
00:02:57,633 --> 00:02:59,146
And then the figures.

53
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:02,387
One to four of them, in the children's words.

54
00:03:02,387 --> 00:03:05,701
Small, dressed in black, with very large eyes.

55
00:03:05,701 --> 00:03:10,599
Some thought of tikoloshes, spirits from Shona and Ndebele folklore.

56
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:13,265
Some of the youngest felt only fear.

57
00:03:13,265 --> 00:03:19,066
Others said the being looked at them, and that they felt it was sad, and that it meant no harm.

58
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:23,661
When the meeting broke up, the children rushed to their teachers.

59
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:27,218
The first reaction, by many accounts, was to dismiss it.

60
00:03:27,218 --> 00:03:28,933
Children and their stories.

61
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:35,858
No one is recorded searching the field that day for a landing mark, or for any physical trace.

62
00:03:35,858 --> 00:03:38,400
There is no photograph of any object.

63
00:03:38,866 --> 00:03:40,293
But the story was out.

64
00:03:40,293 --> 00:03:43,599
By the weekend, it was in the ears of a journalist.

65
00:03:44,066 --> 00:03:44,722
Tape one.

66
00:03:44,722 --> 00:03:47,344
Monday, the nineteenth of September.

67
00:03:47,344 --> 00:03:51,641
A BBC correspondent, Tim Leach, arrives with a camera crew.

68
00:03:51,641 --> 00:03:55,866
The children tell him what they saw, plainly, and on film.

69
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:58,064
The footage is striking.

70
00:03:58,064 --> 00:04:02,102
Children, calm, specific, and not performing for anyone.

71
00:04:02,102 --> 00:04:07,366
Many described a silver craft, black-clad figures, and a feeling of fear.

72
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:10,469
Notice what is missing from tape one.

73
00:04:10,469 --> 00:04:11,252
No message.

74
00:04:11,252 --> 00:04:13,390
Nothing about the environment.

75
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:16,097
No warning about the end of the world.

76
00:04:16,097 --> 00:04:18,733
Just a craft, and beings, and fright.

77
00:04:19,199 --> 00:04:20,229
The report ran.

78
00:04:20,229 --> 00:04:28,533
The story spread, and Ariel became known across the world, a school of sixty-two children and a mystery with no hardware.

79
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,915
Leach said later he was moved.

80
00:04:30,915 --> 00:04:33,660
He said the children were genuinely shaken.

81
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,469
He did not claim to know what they had seen.

82
00:04:36,469 --> 00:04:37,363
Neither do we.

83
00:04:37,363 --> 00:04:39,533
But he had stood in front of them.

84
00:04:39,533 --> 00:04:40,300
That counts.

85
00:04:40,766 --> 00:04:44,593
Tape one, then, gives us children who describe a craft.

86
00:04:44,593 --> 00:04:45,289
Hold that.

87
00:04:45,289 --> 00:04:46,333
On to tape two.

88
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,829
One more thing.

89
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:52,428
Reporters and visiting adults began to collect children's drawings.

90
00:04:52,428 --> 00:04:55,379
A hundred little pictures of one afternoon.

91
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:58,399
The drawings, too, became part of the story.

92
00:04:58,866 --> 00:05:01,972
A car comes down the road the next morning.

93
00:05:01,972 --> 00:05:04,066
A UFO researcher from Harare.

94
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:05,204
Tape two.

95
00:05:05,204 --> 00:05:06,921
Tuesday, the twentieth.

96
00:05:06,921 --> 00:05:14,384
Cynthia Hind, a veteran UFO investigator and the MUFON representative for Africa, visits the school.

97
00:05:14,384 --> 00:05:15,727
The children draw.

98
00:05:15,727 --> 00:05:16,622
She listens.

99
00:05:16,622 --> 00:05:19,533
She is sure they are telling the truth.

100
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,109
There is a catch.

101
00:05:21,109 --> 00:05:27,828
The children were interviewed in small groups of two to six, with the others standing close, listening.

102
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:33,699
Skeptics call it cross-contamination: one child says a detail, and the next one adopts it.

103
00:05:34,166 --> 00:05:37,282
Hind said the pupils all told the same story.

104
00:05:37,282 --> 00:05:38,597
That was her proof.

105
00:05:38,597 --> 00:05:42,197
The skeptic's reply is the same fact, turned around.

106
00:05:42,197 --> 00:05:44,620
Of course they told the same story.

107
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:47,666
They had just been telling it to each other.

108
00:05:48,133 --> 00:05:51,055
A recent article asks a deeper question.

109
00:05:51,055 --> 00:05:57,777
Hind believed rural children in Africa had no television and no alien pictures to draw from.

110
00:05:57,777 --> 00:06:04,499
Yet these were private-school children, in Harare's orbit, with television, films and books.

111
00:06:04,966 --> 00:06:14,038
One researcher has even raised touring puppet shows that visited Zimbabwean schools around then, with strange costumed figures.

112
00:06:14,038 --> 00:06:16,109
It is an idea, not a finding.

113
00:06:16,109 --> 00:06:19,966
But it shows how many ordinary sources there could be.

114
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:22,880
The skeptics add something quieter.

115
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:26,237
In the records, an adult suggests a diving suit.

116
00:06:26,237 --> 00:06:28,964
Later, a child describes a diving suit.

117
00:06:28,964 --> 00:06:34,000
Children are very good at giving adults what they sense the adults want.

118
00:06:34,466 --> 00:06:42,584
Hind interpreted the whole affair this way: the fireball was a real rocket, and an alien craft had come to watch it.

119
00:06:42,584 --> 00:06:45,383
Not a theory every skeptic would accept.

120
00:06:45,383 --> 00:06:47,833
But a theory is exactly what it is.

121
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:52,466
Two months later, a famous American professor lands in Harare.

122
00:06:52,933 --> 00:06:53,742
Tape three.

123
00:06:53,742 --> 00:06:56,021
November, nineteen ninety-four.

124
00:06:56,021 --> 00:07:01,095
John Mack, a Harvard psychiatrist and Pulitzer Prize winner, arrives.

125
00:07:01,095 --> 00:07:06,389
He has spent years studying people who say they were abducted by aliens.

126
00:07:06,389 --> 00:07:07,933
Hind recommended him.

127
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:12,889
He interviews twelve of the children, one at a time and in depth.

128
00:07:12,889 --> 00:07:18,000
The archive will eventually hold more than a hundred pages of transcripts.

129
00:07:18,466 --> 00:07:21,600
And here, on tape three, something new appears.

130
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:25,000
The beings, some children say, passed on a message.

131
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,066
That we are damaging the Earth.

132
00:07:27,066 --> 00:07:29,466
That our technology is poisoning it.

133
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:35,068
One girl is quoted as saying that people must not get too technological.

134
00:07:35,068 --> 00:07:39,633
It is a quiet, strange, and oddly grown-up sentence for a child.

135
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,731
Now compare the tapes.

136
00:07:41,731 --> 00:07:44,252
Tape one, the BBC, has no message.

137
00:07:44,252 --> 00:07:48,479
Tape two, Hind, has no message in the report at the time.

138
00:07:48,479 --> 00:07:53,300
The message appears on tape three, and in only some of the clips.

139
00:07:53,766 --> 00:07:59,006
Of the twelve children Mack interviewed, only seven clips have been made public.

140
00:07:59,006 --> 00:08:01,691
Of those, just three mention the message.

141
00:08:01,691 --> 00:08:04,966
The rest of the record sits in an archive, closed.

142
00:08:05,433 --> 00:08:07,354
The skeptic's case is plain.

143
00:08:07,354 --> 00:08:12,295
Mack was an environmentalist and a believer in the abduction phenomenon.

144
00:08:12,295 --> 00:08:16,823
His own book on the subject had been published only months before.

145
00:08:16,823 --> 00:08:19,500
Critics say he prompted, and suggested.

146
00:08:19,966 --> 00:08:22,061
There is a wider backdrop, too.

147
00:08:22,061 --> 00:08:32,399
The nineteen nineties were thick with alien abduction stories, and in April of that year, a famous abduction hoax had been exposed in the American press.

148
00:08:32,866 --> 00:08:35,677
Mack never claimed the children were lying.

149
00:08:35,677 --> 00:08:39,599
He said they were sincere, and that he could not explain it.

150
00:08:39,599 --> 00:08:41,757
He died in two thousand and four.

151
00:08:41,757 --> 00:08:44,633
The question he raised did not die with him.

152
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,626
The tapes are piling up.

153
00:08:46,626 --> 00:08:49,233
And then, nearly thirty years of silence.

154
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:50,410
Tape four.

155
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:52,543
Two thousand and twenty-three.

156
00:08:52,543 --> 00:08:56,454
A streaming documentary series returns to Ariel School.

157
00:08:56,454 --> 00:09:02,000
It interviews the witnesses, now grown, and the story gets a surprising twist.

158
00:09:02,466 --> 00:09:05,538
One former pupil, Dallyn, says he made it up.

159
00:09:05,538 --> 00:09:10,588
That the boy he was pointed at a shiny rock, and the rest grew from there.

160
00:09:10,588 --> 00:09:11,885
The audience gasps.

161
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,933
The case, it seems, is closed.

162
00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:15,601
But not so fast.

163
00:09:15,601 --> 00:09:19,580
Journalists could not verify the claim independently.

164
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,833
And an old interview surfaces.

165
00:09:22,299 --> 00:09:29,879
A reporter named Nicky Carter had interviewed the same boy two weeks after the event in nineteen ninety-four.

166
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:32,730
Then, he said nothing about making it up.

167
00:09:32,730 --> 00:09:36,833
He described a meteorite-like object seen the night before.

168
00:09:37,299 --> 00:09:42,750
Another interview version places him further away, not seeing the craft at all.

169
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:46,406
Three versions, from one person, across thirty years.

170
00:09:46,406 --> 00:09:48,200
Memory is not a recording.

171
00:09:48,666 --> 00:09:50,333
And remember the numbers.

172
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,733
Sixty-two children said they saw it.

173
00:09:52,733 --> 00:09:57,600
About one hundred and eighty others, by one count, said they saw nothing.

174
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:01,000
Not everyone on that playground saw the same thing.

175
00:10:01,466 --> 00:10:03,921
So tape four does not end the case.

176
00:10:03,921 --> 00:10:07,497
It adds a doubt about one witness, not all of them.

177
00:10:07,497 --> 00:10:08,899
On to the last tape.

178
00:10:09,366 --> 00:10:10,025
Tape five.

179
00:10:10,025 --> 00:10:10,420
Today.

180
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:13,581
The witnesses are in their thirties and forties.

181
00:10:13,581 --> 00:10:16,017
Some have scattered across the world.

182
00:10:16,017 --> 00:10:20,166
Some, like one who has painted the memory, still go back to it.

183
00:10:20,633 --> 00:10:24,179
Many maintain, to this day, that they saw something.

184
00:10:24,179 --> 00:10:26,702
They say the experience changed them.

185
00:10:26,702 --> 00:10:28,952
They say they have never wavered.

186
00:10:28,952 --> 00:10:31,066
That sincerity is not in doubt.

187
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:34,359
But sincerity is not evidence of a craft.

188
00:10:34,359 --> 00:10:39,529
It tells us that something happened inside those children's minds that day.

189
00:10:39,529 --> 00:10:42,699
What that something was, the tapes cannot say.

190
00:10:43,166 --> 00:10:48,733
Mack's archive was donated to a university in two thousand and twenty-three.

191
00:10:48,733 --> 00:10:51,151
It is not yet open to the public.

192
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:54,227
When it opens, it may settle a great deal.

193
00:10:54,227 --> 00:10:55,033
Or nothing.

194
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:56,633
The tapes are in.

195
00:10:56,633 --> 00:10:58,100
Time to mark the case.

196
00:10:58,566 --> 00:10:59,261
Scorecard.

197
00:10:59,261 --> 00:11:02,666
Time to mark the Ariel School case, tape by tape.

198
00:11:03,133 --> 00:11:07,070
Sixty-two children gave sincere accounts: evidence.

199
00:11:07,070 --> 00:11:10,543
A rocket re-entry two days earlier: evidence.

200
00:11:10,543 --> 00:11:13,091
Accounts that agree: only partly.

201
00:11:13,091 --> 00:11:17,799
A telepathic message: appears only on tape three, unverified.

202
00:11:18,266 --> 00:11:20,586
A physical landing mark: none.

203
00:11:20,586 --> 00:11:22,906
Photographs or hardware: none.

204
00:11:22,906 --> 00:11:24,452
Official file: none.

205
00:11:24,452 --> 00:11:27,158
The Netflix confession: unverified.

206
00:11:27,158 --> 00:11:29,633
Alien craft: no evidence at all.

207
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:30,948
The verdict.

208
00:11:30,948 --> 00:11:31,584
Unproven.

209
00:11:31,584 --> 00:11:34,835
The children were real, and so was their fear.

210
00:11:34,835 --> 00:11:44,166
But the record is contaminated by group interviews, by a fireball two days before, and by adults who came with a story of their own.

211
00:11:44,166 --> 00:11:45,933
Nothing physical remains.

212
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:50,452
And yet something unusual did happen on that playground.

213
00:11:50,452 --> 00:11:53,275
Sixty-two children would not forget it.

214
00:11:53,275 --> 00:11:56,966
Let that stand, even as the explanation stays open.

215
00:11:57,433 --> 00:11:59,797
What do you think those children saw?

216
00:11:59,797 --> 00:12:04,399
A rocket, a rumour, a prank, or something we do not yet have a name for?

217
00:12:04,399 --> 00:12:05,933
Tell us in the comments.

218
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:12,107
Next case: an ancient mystery in the desert, and a discovery that will not stay quiet.

219
00:12:12,107 --> 00:12:13,633
We open that file next.

220
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:19,466
Subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test, and come back to the archive.
